design.summary:
v7 keeps the user's core design: two independent grids isolated by magic number (BUY and SELL), and one shared TP per grid set at the live volume-weighted average entry +/- TP and recomputed from live positions after every fill. v7 changes that design from an open-ended averaging machine into a sequence of finite cycles, each with a known loss limit. Every basket now has three barriers, in the order they were added for survival:
(1) A hard time barrier measured from the oldest open position. No adds after 15 min, the TP shrinks from 10 min, and everything is closed at 30 min (configurable 1-30).
(2) A price stop fixed relative to layer 1 at 3 x sigma15, placed before the first fill. It is backed by a broker-side SL on every ticket.
(3) A pre-trade ladder simulation that removes layers until the worst case fits a dollar budget.
That budget is the smaller of 3.5% of equity and a drawdown-floor (CPPI) cushion. Above the budget sit a daily limit (6%), a cap of 2 stops per day, a weekly limit (10%) and a hard kill at -20% from peak.

The lot ladder starts at 0.01. It may step up once to 0.02 on layer 3, and the hard caps are 0.04 lots per side, 0.08 in total and 0.03 net. On a $100 standard account the 0.01 minimum lot leaves room for only 2-3 layers, so the budget check usually trims the step-up away. Every source sweep agrees that per-layer escalation is where grids die (inference plus citations below).

The other filters cut the number of baskets that reach the stop. They are:
- session windows: quiet Asia first, with rollover, the London open and the London fix blacked out;
- a news filter that now also freezes adds, flattens 5 minutes before the event, and refuses any basket whose 30-minute window would overlap an event;
- spacing and TP scaled by volatility, with cost floors;
- a breaker on volatility expansion and price jumps;
- a minimum time between adds, with adds triggered on closed M1 bars;
- skew of the shared inventory across the two grids;
- an optional stretch-based entry trigger.

Plainly: the research and our own Oanda M1 statistics say the gross 5-30 minute snap-back on EURUSD is only about +0.15 to +0.5 pip, against roughly 0.8-1.4 pip of round-trip cost. These changes can turn "blow up the account" into "lose at most about 12-20%, then stop". They do not create edge. The design should be deployed live only if the fully stopped, fully costed version is net positive out of sample. That probably requires a raw-spread or cent account, leverage of 1:200 or more, and trading only in the measured mean-reverting windows.

modifications.what:
Replace AllowedHours with SessionWindowsUTC, a list of HH:MM-HH:MM ranges converted with ServerGMTOffset plus an explicit DST rule. Do not rely on TimeGMT() in the tester.
(a) A new L1 is allowed only if now is in a window AND now <= window_end - MaxHoldMin.
(b) No adds after window_end - 10 min.
(c) At window_end, close any basket still open.
(d) Hard blackouts override the windows:
- RolloverBlackoutUTC 19:00-23:15 (summer; shift 1 h in winter via DST);
- LondonOpenVetoUTC 06:45-08:30;
- London fix 15:55-16:10 London local time, double length at month-end;
- ECB reference fix 13:05-13:25 UTC;
- Monday before 01:00 UTC;
- Friday after FridayLastEntryUTC 19:00.
(e) Default windows: '00:30-05:00' only. Test '08:30-11:30' (allowed only if the M9 ratio < 1.5 and price is back inside the Asian range) and '15:15-18:45' as separate candidates. Each window must pass the per-window validation in the validation plan before it is enabled.
With the 30-min cap this also makes swap structurally zero.

EntryMode: 0 = SYMMETRIC (v6 behaviour: on a new EntryTF bar, when idle and the gates pass, open both grids); 1 = STRETCH.
In STRETCH mode, on each closed M1 bar compute z = (close - EMA(close, ZEmaBars)) / sigma15.
BUY grid L1 opens only if all of these hold:
- z <= -ZEntry;
- the just-closed bar is a reclaim (close > open, and close > the previous bar's low);
- the trend veto passes: |sum of the last 60 r1m| / (sigma1m x sqrt(60)) < TrendTMax, and ADX(M15,14) < ADXMax with hysteresis to ADXMax - 5;
- all M4-M9 gates pass.
SELL mirrors this. The signal stays valid for SignalValidBars.
The two grids remain independent with separate magics: a SELL can start while a BUY is open if its own stretch fires, subject to M11.
EntryTF applies to SYMMETRIC mode (M1 or M5).

Persist per-basket records: open time, close reason (TP / TP-decayed / time / stop / news / breaker / session-end), layers, lots, P/L net of all costs, MAE, realised spread and slippage.
Show on the panel and alert on any of:
- DDR = max equity DD / max balance DD > 2;
- any basket loss > 1.2 x its planned Worst (model breach);
- rolling 200-fill average cost > 1.5 x the model CostPips, which also blocks new grids until reviewed.

Per SessionWindow, over the last EdgeWindowBaskets baskets:
- p_hat = share of baskets that are net winners;
- W = average win and L = average loss, both net and realised (including time and stop exits);
- p_be = L / (W + L);
- p_LCB = Wilson 95% lower bound of p_hat.
Disable the window (block new L1) if the rolling net expectancy < 0, or if p_LCB < p_be once at least 100 baskets are logged. Re-enable only by manual input. Never increase size from this statistic. Use it as a go/no-go gate only; it is not Kelly sizing.

validation_plan:
Acceptance criteria, all must pass in every OOS fold:
- net PF > 1.15 after costs;
- max equity DD <= 20%;
- DDR <= 2;
- worst basket <= 1.2x its planned Worst;
- average loss / average win <= 6, because the design deliberately has small TPs, but the Wilson LB of the basket win rate must be above p_be;
- daily-limit hits <= 2 per month;
- no kill-latch hit outside gap events;
- WFE >= 0.5.
Report how many baskets ended on TP, decayed TP, time stop, price stop, news, breaker and session end.

Robustness:
- Monte Carlo with spread x1.25/x1.5 and slippage x2;
- bootstrap of basket P&L blocks, requiring P(equity DD > 20% within 1 year) < 5%;
- parameter-neighbourhood test: +/-20% on each optimised parameter keeps PF > 1.05.

MT5 confirmation:
- run the final candidates in the Strategy Tester with 'Every tick based on real ticks' on the target broker's history (quality >= 99%), with commission set, Random delay on and the CSV news calendar;
- also run in 1-minute OHLC mode. If OHLC looks better than real ticks, mark the candidate timing-fragile and reject it;
- check that simulator and MT5 basket counts and P&L agree to within about 10%.
